visit (walk.rs:226-290) works as follows:
- it pops parents whose path plus '/' is not a prefix;
- it chains the parent's MatchInfo into matches_using_parent;
- it skips an excluded directory unless may_reinclude_below says otherwise;
- it never reports an excluded entry;
- it reports a held-back excluded ancestor only when a non-excluded descendant is found, outermost first, as fsutil's calledFn loop does.
Paths are relative, built with '/' and compared as bytes, and names are sorted bytewise. Context::walk and Context::matcher (source.rs:185-199) pass the compiled matcher straight through.

The following match BuildKit v0.34.0 as cited:
- trim_continuation (the regex port), directive parsing, comment handling inside continuations and heredoc detection through the shell lexer;
- --network and --security values, which are case-sensitive closed enums (mount.rs:136-190);
- flag parsing: duplicate and unknown flags are rejected (flags.rs:66-125);
- secret mount checks (mount.rs:343-356).
Where ranikust departs from BuildKit, it is stricter:
- the ONBUILD depth cap;
- the COPY --from stage index, where BuildKit's image-index accident is not kept;
- shell substitution depth.
A flag that ranikust fails to recognise stays part of the command and is never granted. Entitlement handling of --security, --network=host and --device is in peer-owned stage.rs.
layers_needed and squash_for_shared_root keep a stage that is only COPY --from'd or mounted out of the walked or pushed set (squash.rs:121-188). Checked by hand on the build-secrets-then-COPY --from pattern.

Ported behaviours:
- a line over 65535 bytes, counting its CR, is an error (ignorefile.rs:15,45);
- one CR before LF or at EOF is dropped, as bufio dropCR does;
- the BOM is stripped on the first line only;
- '#' is a comment only at column 0;
- TrimSpace, then '!' and TrimSpace again;
- filepath.Clean (golang.rs clean);
- a leading '/' is stripped only when more follows.
The error propagates through rnk-context Context::matcher (source.rs:185-194) as Error::Ignore. No fallback treats a broken ignore file as an empty one. lib.rs: Error::LineTooLong, BadPattern and IllegalExclusion are all hard errors, and the crate never touches the filesystem.

The following equal patternmatcher New, MatchesOrParentMatches, MatchesUsingParentResults and Pattern.match:
- Matcher::new (matcher.rs:88-125): trim, Clean, '!' handling, the lone-'!' error, and validation with filepath.Match(p, ".");
- matches_or_parent_matches and matches_using_parent (matcher.rs:140-213): the 'exclusion != matched' skip, the per-pattern parent_matched chaining, and the parent-directory fallback only without parent info;
- Exact, Prefix and Suffix matching, including the '**/foo' matches 'foo' case.
A pattern that fails to compile is stored as Err and reported when it is first evaluated, as with Go's lazy compile, so the walk fails rather than skipping the pattern.

should_escape (matcher.rs:278) escapes only .+()$, which matches the vendored patternmatcher v0.6.1 (../buildkit/vendor/github.com/moby/patternmatcher/patternmatcher.go:24-31). There, escapeBytes[b%8] |= 1<<(b/8) overflows for '|', '{' and '}', which therefore reach the regexp unescaped. Groups can come only from '(.*/)?', because '(' and ')' are escaped. The goregexp parser rejects what Go rejects:
- '(?';
- stacked repeats (goregexp.rs:225);
- {n,m} counts above 1000 (goregexp.rs:149);
- bad escapes, ranges and \C.
It also keeps Go semantics:
- ClassNL: negated classes match \n;
- OneLine: ^ and $ anchor at the ends of the text;
- ASCII \b, \d, \s and \w;
- POSIX and Unicode tables.
Literals are emitted as \x{..} and classes as explicit ranges. The upstream-derived tests and the 'checked against Go' cases (matcher/tests.rs:428-460) cover the quirks. No differential that includes a path BuildKit excludes was found.

Holds. These directory descriptors exist during a Direct RUN:
- the state directory: an O_PATH directory, an O_RDONLY flock descriptor and a RootPath (store.rs:353-376);
- kaniko Shared.root on / and Shared.kept on the state directory (kaniko/root.rs:166-187);
- the root_lock flock on / (setup.rs:276, 317);
- the local context RootPath (rnk-context source.rs:87-90; tar, git and HTTPS contexts are unsupported).
All of them are on the container's own mount tree, and a root RUN reaches them by path. While a RUN runs, the state directory holds no name: enter_run brackets Sandbox::run (stage.rs:798-821), and O_TMPFILE or unlinked files cannot be listed. COPY --from views exist only inside a fence window, and Direct refuses bind, tmpfs and ssh mounts (mounts.rs:263-303). walk.rs:533 holds /proc/self/fd only during the walk, never while a RUN runs. procfs checks ptrace access when an entry is used, so a cwd in a procfs directory would add nothing. A cwd from the magic link gains nothing over path access.
